0 20.5 13Z"/></svg></button></div></header><header><strong>ATTENTION &amp; SENTIMENT</strong><nav><a href="index.html">Wiki hub</a><a href="crowding-tracker.html">Market radar</a><a href="narrative-diffusion.html">Muse case</a><a href="cnn-next-week.html">Market extremes</a></nav></header><main id="research-main" tabindex="-1">
<div class="intro"><div><div class="eyebrow">Specialist sales · 07–21 Sep 2026</div><h1>What investors believe.<br>What they may already own.</h1><p>Company debates, expectations and reported positioning — with source disagreements and gaps in coverage visible.</p></div><span class="pill">Private research · contextual review</span></div>
<div id="stats" class="stats"></div><div id="coverage" class="card pad"></div>
<div class="split space"><article class="card"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Five crowding questions</div><h2>Strong stories, a high expectations bar</h2><p>Explicit crowded-long language in reviewed company passages.</p></div></div><div id="crowding-list"></div></article><article class="card"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Five skepticism questions</div><h2>Low enthusiasm, shorts or fading conviction</h2><p>Different forms of skepticism; an operating catalyst is still needed.</p></div></div><div id="skepticism-list"></div></article></div><p class="muted" style="font-size:12px;margin:10px 2px">Editorial research priorities, not a numerical ranking, a buy/sell signal or a measured weekly change. Select a name to inspect its evidence.</p>
<div class="split space"><article class="card"><div class="section-head"><div><h2>Where preferences shifted</h2><p>Barclays survey · share choosing a preferred long (%)</p></div><div class="toolbar" id="survey-tabs"></div></div><div id="survey" class="survey pad" style="padding-top:0"></div><div id="survey-note" class="note"></div></article><article class="card"><div class="section-head"><div><h2>Conviction ≠ ownership</h2><p>Categorical map of reviewed direct commentary. Click a ticker.</p></div></div><div id="matrix" class="signal-matrix"></div><div class="note">No continuous score is implied by these cells. Opposing desk accounts remain in “Divergent”; operating-only and uncovered names appear in the company explorer below.</div></article></div>
<section id="explorer" class="space" style="scroll-margin-top:20px"><div class="intro"><div><div class="eyebrow">Full coverage ledger</div><h2>Explore all 106 companies</h2></div><div class="toolbar"><button class="choice" id="export">Coverage CSV ↓</button><button class="choice" id="reset">Reset filters</button></div></div><div class="explore"><article class="card"><div class="pad toolbar"><input id="search" class="choice" type="search" placeholder="Ticker, company or debate…" aria-label="Search company" style="width:100%"><select id="coverage-filter" class="choice" aria-label="Coverage filter"><option>All coverage</option><option>Direct desk view</option><option>Context only</option><option>Coverage gap</option><option>Desk disagreements</option></select><select id="house-filter" class="choice" aria-label="Source house"><option>All houses</option></select></div><div id="table-count" class="head-count" aria-live="polite"></div><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Company</th><th>Desk tone</th><th>Reported positioning</th><th>Sources</th></tr></thead><tbody id="company-table"></tbody></table></div></article><article class="card" id="company-panel" aria-live="polite"></article></div></section>
<section class="space"><div class="section-head" style="padding-left:0"><div><h2>The market backdrop behind the single names</h2><p>Aggregate desk/PB observations have a different population from company-specific client conversations.</p></div></div><div id="macro" class="three"></div></section>
<details class="card pad method space"><summary>How to read this research — coverage, attribution and the next improvement</summary><div id="method"></div><p><b>The next measurable step:</b> preserve each newly received observation with its knowledge timestamp, author, investor group, event and explicit position/flow language. Compare the same desks through time, then test whether new independent interest precedes 5/20-session excess returns. Retrospective commentary from after a rally must never enter the pre-rally feature set.</p><p><b>Source boundaries:</b> reported investor positions are observations from a desk’s client sample. They are not audited fund holdings. Poll percentages are not ownership percentages. A repeated narrative or a forward remains one underlying observation, and a research relay is not a new sales vote.</p></details>
<footer><span>Sources: retained Outlook specialist/sector-sales emails · original dates and links preserved</span><span>Experimental research · no leading relationship established</span></footer></main><noscript><p class="empty">Enable JavaScript to inspect the company evidence. The downloadable coverage CSV is also available beside this dashboard.</p></noscript><script id="specialist-data" type="application/json">{"meta":{"reviewed_at":"2026-09-21T23:26:27.396208+00:00","window_start":"2026-09-07","window_end":"2026-09-21","universe":106,"screened_candidates":248,"screened_houses":9,"selected_sources_reviewed":41,"reviewed_observations":155,"companies_with_context":90,"companies_with_direct_view":63,"coverage_gaps":16,"new_email_bodies":103,"reused_deliveries":241,"scope":"Selected relevant passages across known specialist/sector-sales senders, including corroborating and contradictory views. Candidate screening is broader than contextual review; attachments, embedded images and every mailbox sender are not exhaustively reviewed.","dedup":"Same sender + normalized subject + UTC delivery date across caches; one source house per firm. Different days can repeat the same narrative and are not treated as independent votes.","time_rule":"Email receipt time is retained. Forwarded/prior-period remarks retain their described horizon; no historical knowledge-availability ledger exists. This snapshot is descriptive and cannot be used as a point-in-time backtest.","labels":"Desk tone is a categorical synthesis of reviewed direct views (recent 14–21 Sep where available, otherwise earlier window). Mixed preserves opposing arguments. Research/news/management relays cannot populate desk tone or positioning. No new numerical crowding score is fitted.","highlight_rule":"Five editorial research priorities per group, selected from explicit company-level passages. Not a quantitative rank, buy/sell recommendation or measured weekly change.","false_matches_rejected":["Meta Marshall ≠ META","Tokyo Electron / TEL ≠ TE Connectivity","Deutsche Telekom / DT ≠ Dynatrace","Eaton fire ≠ Eaton","BE Semiconductor ≠ Bloom Energy","Adobe C\u0026MP ≠ MP Materials"]},"companies":{"AAOI":{"ticker":"AAOI","name":"APPLIED OPTOELECTRONICS INC","coverage":"Coverage gap","tone":"No desk view","position":"Not established","summary":"No substantive company-specific specialist passage found in the screened sender/window sample.","summary_source":null,"latest":null,"latest_direct":null,"houses":[],"desk_houses":[],"notes":0,"observations":[],"disagreement":null,"watch":"Obtain substantive specialist commentary before assigning any sentiment or positioning label.","gap_reason":"No substantive company-specific specialist passage found in the screened sender/window sample."},"AAPL":{"ticker":"AAPL","name":"APPLE INC","coverage":"Direct desk view","tone":"Cautious","position":"Not established","summary":"The specialist questions the recent outperformance and sees limited incremental upside given intensifying supply-chain costs.","summary_source":"5eba7d81365d","latest":"2026-09-20T15:02:15Z","latest_direct":"2026-09-20T15:02:15Z","houses":["JPMorgan","UBS"],"desk_houses":["UBS"],"notes":2,"observations":[{"ticker":"AAPL","source":"5eba7d81365d","kind":"Desk view","tone":"Cautious","position":"Not stated","summary":"The specialist questions the recent outperformance and sees limited incremental upside given intensifying supply-chain costs.","id":"obs-089","date":"2026-09-20T15:02:15Z","excerpt":"…P, AAPL, and HPQ) most are puzzled by the recent outperformance (me too…) and don’t see the incremental upside from currently levels as the supply chain challenges likely intensify into C’27. However, if are you are compelled to put new money to work here we still like SNX for the Hyve business. \n\nLooking ahead, investor focus shifts to the September 24 Trump-Xi summit, where potential developments around AI governan…","review":"Assistant contextual review; not independently validated"},{"ticker":"AAPL","source":"f6cda4e37973","kind":"Research relay","tone":"Improving","position":"Not stated","summary":"Chatterjee’s follow-up finds expanding lead times that moderate initial demand concerns. This is an operating check, distinct from still-cautious desk sentiment.","id":"obs-102","date":"2026-09-17T13:37:18Z","excerpt":"…eet up!\n\n## \n\n## Key Research Highlights \u0026 Spec Commentary\n\n**_AAPL: Product Availability Tracker – Strong Mid-week Expansion in Lead Times Moderates Demand Concerns._** Here\n\nFor years, Samik Chatterjee's AAPL iPhone launch product availability tracker has been a helpful investor resource. His first mid- week availability check shows iPhone 18 Pro lead times have expanded by 12 days and Pro Max by 7 d…","review":"Assistant contextual review; not independently validated"}],"disagreement":null,"watch":"What company-specific evidence would change this view, and is new interest turning into new long buying or only covering?","gap_reason":null},"AGX":{"ticker":"AGX","name":"ARGAN INC","coverage":"Context only","tone":"No desk view","position":"Not established","summary":"The construction conference recap includes Argan within strong multi-year end markets, with execution, labor and prefab as margin drivers. It provides no Argan-specific investor-positioning evidence.","summary_source":"a4be3edffc34","latest":"2026-09-18T20:17:50Z","latest_direct":null,"houses":["Jefferies"],"desk_houses":[],"notes":1,"observations":[{"ticker":"AGX","source":"a4be3edffc34","kind":"Research relay","tone":"Positive","position":"Not stated","summary":"The construction conference recap includes Argan within strong multi-year end markets, with execution, labor and prefab as margin drivers. It provides no Argan-specific investor-positioning evidence.","id":"obs-109","date":"2026-09-18T20:17:50Z","excerpt":"…n not bid-margins. Prefab a big initiative. Strategic M\u0026A in focus. Craft labor an advantage. End-markets strength drive multi-year growth. See AGX, ECG, MYRG, MWH summaries.\n\n**Taking The Pulse: What’s Ailing E\u0026C?** The Specialty E\u0026C sector relative valuations have essentially erased the relative peak-high valuation set back in May and now near historical levels. We summarize key are…","review":"Assistant contextual review; not independently validated"}],"disagreement":null,"watch":"Seek a dated specialist view on investor expectations and positioning; current operating/research context alone does not establish crowding.","gap_reason":null},"AMD":{"ticker":"AMD","name":"ADVANCED MICRO DEVICES","coverage":"Direct desk view","tone":"Mixed","position":"Divergent reports","summary":"Fundamental enthusiasm remains, but valuation/ramp concerns for AMD and COT/MediaTek competition for AVGO push both into the tactical funding-short camp in this sample.","summary_source":"5eba7d81365d","latest":"2026-09-20T15:02:15Z","latest_direct":"2026-09-20T15:02:15Z","houses":["Barclays","UBS"],"desk_houses":["Barclays","UBS"],"notes":2,"observations":[{"ticker":"AMD","source":"5eba7d81365d","kind":"Investor feedback","tone":"Mixed","position":"Funding short","summary":"Fundamental enthusiasm remains, but valuation/ramp concerns for AMD and COT/MediaTek competition for AVGO push both into the tactical funding-short camp in this sample.","id":"obs-075","date":"2026-09-20T15:02:15Z","excerpt":"…NTM upside and the ongoing shift to COT and the Mediatek competitive dynamics have kept a lid on AVGO shifting both of these names into the funding short camp for now. As for discovery value as mentioned last week, I continue to field more inquiries and interest in both INTC and QCOM. We struggle to get very excited about QCOM’s opportunity in customer ASIC and more than $18.00 in EPS, but I tend to see…","review":"Assistant contextual review; not independently validated"},{"ticker":"AMD","source":"f1024f160d2a","kind":"Investor feedback","tone":"Positive","position":"Long bias","summary":"Rand lists these as preferred compute longs despite uncertainty about what will re-rate the broader AI trade. This is qualitative client feedback, not the survey result.","id":"obs-046","date":"2026-09-16T11:17:44Z","excerpt":"…he catalyst is for the overall narrative on the AI semis trade to start to turn more positive and what will drive a re-rating in the space. AMD, INTC and MRVL are the preferred names in the space right now on the long side for investors while investors are more cautious on AVGO, NVDA, ARM and CBRS.\n\n* Semicap: In general investors are still positive on the fundamentals of the space, but are not sure how much more upsid…","review":"Assistant contextual review; not independently validated"}],"disagreement":"Barclays prefers AMD in client conversations; UBS later places it in the funding-short camp. The survey shows preference falling versus June. Different dates and samples, not a single consensus.","watch":"What company-specific evidence would change this view, and is new interest turning into new long buying or only covering?","gap_reason":null},"AMZN":{"ticker":"AMZN","name":"AMAZON.COM INC","coverage":"Direct desk view","tone":"Mixed","position":"Not established","summary":"Muse access restrictions brought renewed inbound questions about horizontal-agent disruption. Most clients in this sample were not very worried given Alexa and the delivery network.","summary_source":"cfb4aecc79d0","latest":"2026-09-21T12:15:00Z","latest_direct":"2026-09-21T12:15:00Z","houses":["Bernstein","JPMorgan"],"desk_houses":["Bernstein","JPMorgan"],"notes":3,"observations":[{"ticker":"AMZN","source":"cfb4aecc79d0","kind":"Investor feedback","tone":"Mixed","position":"Not stated","summary":"Muse access restrictions brought renewed inbound questions about horizontal-agent disruption. Most clients in this sample were not very worried given Alexa and the delivery network.","id":"obs-016","date":"2026-09-21T12:15:00Z","excerpt":"…ZN is concerned about the agent capturing customer credentials