 \n\nMedia \u0026 Telecom: \n\n* NFLX: Still a crowded short. Shorts simply ask, ‘Why shouldn’t this trade at 15x-18x forward EPS when Revenue growth is decelerating towards +10%?’ In other words, Bears argue that NFLX should trade at no better than a 1x PEG. And I honestly can’t blame them – not wh…","review":"Assistant contextual review; not independently validated"}],"disagreement":null,"watch":"What new operating catalyst could challenge the short thesis and trigger covering?","gap_reason":null},"NOW":{"ticker":"NOW","name":"SERVICENOW INC","coverage":"Direct desk view","tone":"Constructive","position":"Long bias","summary":"Near the top of preferred application-software longs, but the preference is relative to peers rather than outright investor exuberance.","summary_source":"44c1562e9647","latest":"2026-09-18T11:32:07Z","latest_direct":"2026-09-18T11:32:07Z","houses":["Barclays","JPMorgan"],"desk_houses":["Barclays","JPMorgan"],"notes":2,"observations":[{"ticker":"NOW","source":"44c1562e9647","kind":"Investor feedback","tone":"Positive","position":"Long bias","summary":"Near the top of preferred application-software longs, but the preference is relative to peers rather than outright investor exuberance.","id":"obs-027","date":"2026-09-18T11:32:07Z","excerpt":"…ngs in the app space, but I would still say investor feedback isn’t super bullish on the name, it’s more that investors seeing this name as better positioned than other app names. \n\n* WDAY: Mostly about the potential of a deal right now on the name, but even if a deal was announced investor feedback was that the stock likely wouldn’t trade that much above current levels (~$200). Without the deal, investor feedback …","review":"Assistant contextual review; not independently validated"},{"ticker":"NOW","source":"74a0afba2068","kind":"Investor feedback","tone":"Mixed","position":"Not stated","summary":"The rebound and stabilized cRPO have not yet translated into strong investor bullishness. Separate an im